              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Ramsli is a Hungarian trick-taking game related to French Rams and Croatian Raub. 4-card hands. Donauschwaben (German Danube settlers) version documented by Rick Heli. Declarer vs defenders; bidding; trump."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Hungarian Rams. Donauschwaben 18th-19th c. Rick Heli Card Games of Donauschwaben."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Two or more players."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "A 32-card pack with French suits and ranks from 7 to Ace, as used in the Rams group; one card is turned for trump."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "32-card pack."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "4 each; turn trump."
